If a patient has a taper-progress-failure-despite-opioid-related-harm then every clinician should conduct a DSM-5-opioid-use-disorder-assessment for the patient.
If a patient has a DSM-5-opioid-use-disorder-criteria-match then every clinician should offer an evidence-based-medication-treatment to the patient.
If a patient has a DSM-5-opioid-use-disorder-criteria-match then every clinician should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient.
